# board-smoke

A portable application for a board that carries a panel, a touch controller, an
inertial sensor, and a clock. It names those four interfaces and no board, no
SDK, and no vendor: whichever providers the selected platform binds are the ones
it talks to.

It exists to prove that a board binding four interfaces links all four, which no
single-interface application can show.
